{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChDDcVFcGnaz9ypG9FFwo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no vulnerability in this function and wrote that verdict to `results/s121.json`.\n\n`pmic_glink_send()` takes `pg->state_lock`, checks that `pg->ept` is not NULL, and only then calls `rpmsg_send()`. If the endpoint is missing it returns `-ECONNRESET`. The lock covers both the check and the send, so another thread can't clear or free the endpoint in between.\n\nThis looks like the already-fixed version of the function. An unprotected version that called `rpmsg_send(client->pg->ept, …)` directly would have a race and a possible NULL-pointer dereference while the device is being removed.\n\nOne assumption: the code that tears down the endpoint isn't in this file. The verdict relies on that code clearing `pg->ept` while holding the same `state_lock`, which is the usual pattern in this driver."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":22046,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"output_tokens":280,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eeb9314f-eec0-442b-9a8f-d852e5ab1122","uuid":"ef7d83b7-f1f4-4ccb-b01e-d332d6977953","timestamp":"2026-11-20T00:16:54.903Z","request_id":"req_011ChDDcV7ffyLeraNVSYta2"}
